{
  "id": "L-001",
  "title": "The Idea of a Limit",
  "atom_ids": ["A-01"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The Idea of a Limit" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A limit asks a precise question about a function: what does the output approach as the input gets close to some value? The function does not have to be defined at that value for the limit to exist. The whole point of a limit is to talk about the neighbourhood of a point without ever landing on it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": "Limit (informal)",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We write "
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "source": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = L"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and say the limit of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " approaches "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when the values of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(x)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " get arbitrarily close to "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " gets close to "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", without requiring that "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(a)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " exists or equals "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The canonical example of a function with a limit that is not its value is "
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "source": "g(x) = \\dfrac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". At "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x = 1" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " the formula reads "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "0/0" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", so "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "g(1)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " does not exist. But everywhere else the fraction cancels: "
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "source": "g(x) = x + 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". As "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " approaches 1 from either side, the outputs press in on the value 2."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\dfrac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1} = \\lim_{x \\to 1} (x + 1) = 2",
      "display": true,
      "number": "(1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "figures/limit-approach.png",
      "atom_id": "A-01",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The graph of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "g(x) = \\dfrac{x^2-1}{x-1}" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is the line "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "y = x + 1" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with a hole at "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "(1, 2)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The limit is the y-value the curve approaches, 2, even though the point itself is missing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "widget",
      "name": "plot",
      "version": "1.0",
      "parameters": {
        "series": [
          {
            "label": "g(x) = x + 1 (excluding x = 1)",
            "points": [
              [0.2, 1.2], [0.4, 1.4], [0.6, 1.6], [0.8, 1.8],
              [0.9, 1.9], [0.95, 1.95], [0.99, 1.99],
              [1.01, 2.01], [1.05, 2.05], [1.1, 2.1],
              [1.2, 2.2], [1.4, 2.4], [1.6, 2.6], [1.8, 2.8]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "xlabel": "x",
        "ylabel": "y",
        "title": "Approaching the hole at x = 1"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "note",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The limit is about approach, not arrival. Whether "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(a)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " exists, and what it is if it does, is a separate question answered in step L-003."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "formative",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Suppose "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "h" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is undefined at "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x = 3" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " but the values of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "h(x)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " approach 7 as "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " approaches 3. In your own words, what can you conclude about "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 3} h(x)" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "?" }
      ],
      "kind": "free_response"
    }
  ]
}